       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise substantially, and there's no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory use, for example in rheumatologic conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for analgesia, or **400\u2013800 mg PO three times daily**.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily, if the 1600 was meant as a daily total.\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest a pharmacist or attending review first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
